WEBVTT

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:04.940
He’s still not here? Sheesh!

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.570
Is he coming soon? What’s taking so long?

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.460
What have you been waiting for since this morning?

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.490
The special thing, of course!

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.760
Special thing?

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.760
He’s here!

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.880
What?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.770
Wait!

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.920
Hey, aren’t you supposed to
deliver something to me?

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.840
For Yuma Tsukumo!

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.010
Yuma Tsukumo?

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.600
Hmm...

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.480
Tsukumo...

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.650
Nothing.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.070
There’s no mail for Yuma Tsukumo.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.840
Hey, class rep! How are you?

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.000
It’s too early to be so excited!

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.960
Did something good happen to you?

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.550
Of course! This!

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.540
It’s starting!

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.930
The World Duel Carnival!

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.660
Heartland is sponsoring a world duel tournament!

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.940
The preliminaries finally begin tomorrow!

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:32.530
The top prize is a free lifetime passport to Heartland and the title as the first duel champion!

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:40.740
And Mr. Heartland will grant the winner one wish!

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.740
Incredible!

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:46.460
If I win, I’m going to wish for a hundred wishes.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.920
I don’t think that’s allowed.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.630
If I win, Yuma and I will...

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.580
Is everyone participating?

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:00.170
Of course. Look.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:00.970
What’s that?

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.140
A Heart Piece. It’s a piece of a heart.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.040
This is the passport to the Duel Carnival!

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:07.880
I have one too!

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:08.940
Same here!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.010
Everyone has one.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.730
Oh really?

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:17.650
Yuma, what’s wrong?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.470
I don’t have one.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.380
Don’t have what?

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.240
Why?

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.880
Why am I the only one
who didn’t get a Heart Piece?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.490
Damn!

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.170
Yuma, you don’t want to
participate in the Duel Carnival?

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.150
It’s not that I don’t want to! I can’t!

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:43.100
Why is Yuma the only one who didn’t get one?

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:43.850
That’s strange.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.570
Does Astral have something to say about this?

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.240
It’s because Yuma is an idiot.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:54.150
Be quiet! No one thinks I’m a duelist!

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.110
Did you apply properly?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.340
What?

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:01.860
Did you send your Duel
Carnival application?

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.140
There’s an application?

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.080
Yes. Look.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.310
You have to click here to apply.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:14.010
They don’t send a Heart Piece to every duelist?

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.840
Of course not!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.040
Duelists from around the world are participating.

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.510
I see.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.470
You’re so careless.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:25.440
You would’ve known if you thought about it.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.180
It’s just like your dueling.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.640
Yuma!

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:32.480
Why don’t you apply now?

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.820
I’ll do that!

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.410
Address and name... Yeah, I know.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.070
All right!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:43.360
The entry deadline has passed.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.580
What?

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.870
Thank you for so many entries!

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.210
Yuma, where are you going?

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.310
Why are you running?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.180
I’m running for the Duel Carnival!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.900
I can never understand you.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.360
You’re also participating
in the Duel Carnival, right?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.760
No.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.320
I no longer want glory on the big stage.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.910
Shark...

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:29.390
I’ll duel for myself.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.460
I see.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.620
See ya.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.790
Yuma!

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.370
Shark?

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.470
Yeah.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.300
It’s been awhile, Ryoga.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:09.020
Or should I call you Shark?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.540
You!

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.000
What’s the meaning of this?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.880
I’m just saying hello before the Duel Carnival.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.960
I’m not entering the tournament.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.630
Oh really.

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.570
You still can’t get over that incident?

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:26.130
What?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.290
I’ll tell you an interesting story.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:35.690
During the finals, you looked at my deck in the waiting room and were disqualified.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:41.980
But you weren’t in the right frame of mind.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:47.660
Someone dear to you was
in an unfortunate accident.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.790
Ryoga, you must win.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.790
I’m fine...

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:05.670
While you’re in that mental state, what would happen if your opponent intentionally laid out his deck?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.520
What if the girl’s accident wasn’t an accident?

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.340
You...

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.980
You did that to trap me!

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.440
How dare you?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.400
You must not resort to violence.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.070
It makes me laugh.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:32.580
Due to that incident, you were banished from the dueling spotlight.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:36.770
Meanwhile, I’m the duel champion of the Far East.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:38.940
There’s a huge gap between us.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.800
It must be frustrating.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:41.880
How dare you?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.300
Then try to defeat me in the Duel Carnival!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.540
I’ll be waiting for you.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.450
The World Duel Carnival...

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.960
I reached my hand towards

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.140
The light that shines to tomorrow

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:08.030
I dreamed of the world that spreads beneath my feet

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:17.290
I don’t know where dreams and hope are located

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:21.870
No matter how much I search, I can’t find them

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:28.000
Maybe it fell into the space between truth and lies

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:33.090
Our story hasn’t started yet

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:38.500
The road to tomorrow seems like it will crumble

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.980
But let’s go before we lose heart

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.440
As we come closer, it moves further away

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.820
In order to seize the truth

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:55.450
We’ll search for hope in the unseen future

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.240
Our hearts are stronger than everyone else’s

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:01.830
We’ll carry it within us and go

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:07.040
Fight weakness to have the strength to win

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.280
In order to find it

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.470
Along with my irreplaceable friends

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:19.060
I saw tomorrow in the world that spreads beneath my feet

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:37.160
\hThe World Duel Carnival Starts!\h

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:37.160
Number 26:

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.540
Ryoga will participate
in the Duel Carnival, like you wanted.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.950
Thanks for your help.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.720
But why do you care about him?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.390
As a duelist, he’s an empty shell.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:04.690
But I still need him when we gather all the Numbers.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:11.340
Fine. I’ll enjoy dropping him into hell again.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.780
Can you please do something?

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.230
I’ve come all the way to Heartland!

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:25.750
There’s nothing I can do.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.560
That’s why I’m asking you to something!

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.420
If I don’t enter the Duel Carnival, I’m going to die!

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.210
See? My pulse...

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:39.300
Oh no! I’m dying!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:44.100
Thank you for coming today.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.900
Hey!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.780
Hand over a Heart Piece!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:57.490
He’s like an annoying drunk.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.900
This is an announcement.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:13.630
Passengers who haven’t boarded Flights #719 and #441, please come to the check-in counter.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:31.810
Thank you for using the monorail today.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.080
Heartland City’s population increased by 158%.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.570
Increasing by 5% every hour.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.180
They’re here!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:46.510
They’re excited for the Duel Carnival!

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.250
Are there any problems in any section?

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.880
All security cameras functioning normally.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.560
No problems with network transmissions.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.380
All traffic obots operating normally.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.710
I’m fired up! I’m excited!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.310
What’s the point of you being excited, Gauche?

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:11.710
As the management committee, we provide surveillance for the Duel Carnival.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:12.810
You must always remain calm.

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.530
You never get excited.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:21.340
Dolowa, I guess it’s impossible for a cold-blooded woman like you to get excited.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:21.980
What?

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.980
Stop arguing.

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:27.220
The preparations are proceeding smoothly.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.810
Kaito.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.380
I’ve been waiting for you.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:35.670
Why did you call me?

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.610
Call you?

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:42.380
I wanted you to see this before the Carnival begins.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:49.390
Many duelists have gathered
in Heartland City for the Carnival.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:54.770
Among these duelists,
some will definitely have Numbers.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:12:01.780
Winning during the Carnival is the same as taking Numbers from those duelists.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.920
But don’t let your guard down.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:07.700
According to my info, powerful duelists from around the world have entered.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:11.210
Don’t worry.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:15.290
If you can’t do it,
I’ll gather the Numbers.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.960
No one is skilled enough to oppose me.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.010
Well said, Kaito. How reassuring.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.740
Stop it, Gauche.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.390
Mr. Heartland!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:28.600
There’s a boy at the front
gate who wants to participate.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.390
Send him away.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:34.510
But he won’t go home
until he gets a Heart Piece.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:37.650
He’s like an annoying drunk.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.050
Drunk?

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:43.360
It’s my once-in-a-lifetime request!
Give me a Heart Piece!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.650
That guy...

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.410
Hurry up and send him away!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:46.820
Right!

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.290
Wait! Let him participate.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.790
You know him?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:56.290
No, but he may have a Number.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:13:00.460
Kaito, are you keeping secrets from me?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:04.930
There was a mysterious explosion at Heartland’s facility the other day.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.810
That was a machine malfunction.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.680
As long as I’m gathering Numbers,
you shouldn’t be complaining.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:14.390
I’m not required to report everything I do to you.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.150
Fine.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:22.990
Master Kaito, you’re not going to report your incident with Yuma Tsukumo?

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.450
It’s none of your business!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:26.950
Understood!

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.830
If I do have an enemy, it’s...

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:31.740
Astral.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:35.540
I promise to defeat him!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:38.370
No way! You think Yuma Tsukumo is your rival?

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.940
No, Yuma Tsukumo is...

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.710
Yuma Tsukumo is what?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.800
An idiot.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:49.480
I won’t go home until I get a Heart Piece!

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.580
Will he get a Heart Piece acting that way?

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:53.860
Who knows.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.570
What?

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:12.770
He’s...

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:14.410
Mr. Heartland!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.160
It’s really him!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.050
Old man!

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:27.320
Old man?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:30.020
C’mon, Yuma!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.630
It’s the honorable Mr. Heartland!

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:34.370
Yeah yeah, Heartland.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.500
Mister!

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.640
Yeah, Mr. Heartland.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:38.730
The honorable!

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:43.810
Anyway, the Duel Carnival’s homepage is confusing.

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:50.660
It was confusing, so I didn’t know
that I had to click to apply.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.680
He doesn’t know when to give up.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:57.370
Can’t he just say that he made a mistake?

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.850
I understand.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:04.440
Your wish has touched my passionate heart.

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.380
I will grant you your wish.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:15.060
This is a Heart Piece!

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.390
Hooray!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:22.310
That pendant...

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.060
This?

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.080
It’s a unique shape.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:28.530
It’s a memento from my mom and dad.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.980
Memento?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:35.770
I recall seeing that pendant somewhere.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:43.920
It’s time to fulfill the promise you made with your dad.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:47.250
You promised to become duel champion.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.290
Yeah!

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.760
Yuma.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:52.220
You must win.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:57.450
Since it’s a huge tournament, many duelists that have Numbers will participate.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:00.230
If we retrieve those Numbers...

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:03.940
Yeah. You’ll regain your memories.

00:16:04.340 --> 00:16:09.400
But Astral, I’m not going to obsess about winning this tournament.

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:14.040
What do you mean?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.330
That means you’ll be contradicting the promise you made with your father.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.040
I’ve been thinking for a long time.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:24.500
About what dueling means to me.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:29.800
I lost all the time before I met you,
but I can now defeat powerful enemies.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:37.260
And when I dueled against Shark and Kaito,
I learned that there’s something you lose by losing.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:41.180
But I never hated dueling.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.800
That’s right.

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.730
Winning or losing a duel doesn’t matter to me.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:48.190
I don’t know how to say it, but...

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.150
For me, dueling is a bond!

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:52.820
Bond?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.320
Yeah! I want to bond with everyone I duel.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.120
Winning or losing doesn’t matter.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.000
Dueling and competing are different things.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.590
Dueling and competing are different...

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.480
But if you lose, I’ll vanish.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.380
I can’t accept your point-of-view.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.730
I know how you feel.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:15.090
I’ll do anything to save you.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:20.570
But I now know that there’s something more important than winning or losing a duel.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:25.350
There’s something more valuable
than winning and losing!

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:27.560
Then what will you do about Kaito?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.310
Kaito...

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:29.440
That’s right.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:34.030
He’ll challenge you to a duel
without caring about your beliefs.

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.740
Kaito...

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:40.450
If I lose, he might take my soul.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:44.080
But I won’t change my dueling. I’ll battle him.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.250
Yuma...

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.170
Kotori?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:51.170
If your soul gets taken, I’ll...

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.480
I’ll...

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:56.880
Don’t worry! I won’t lose to him!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:01.810
I’ll win! I promise I’ll win!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:03.560
You’re right.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:08.480
You won’t listen to me even if I tried to stop you. And you also have Astral.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:14.200
But if you’re going to enter, you must win!

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:15.590
Understood?

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.700
Yes!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:24.520
Something more valuable than winning and losing...

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.600
Should I use these?
I’m not sure...

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:42.620
I wonder if everyone
is also building their decks.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.650
It’s finally starting.

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:16.110
Yeah!

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:19.330
I can’t wait to show my skills! Therefore...

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:20.680
Therefore?

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:24.830
I’ll win with Osaka granny power!

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:29.300
Maa, if I win, I’ll buy you Bermuda pants.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:32.120
What are you talking about? And who’s Maa?

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:41.300
Duelists in Heartland City,
I’ll explain the Duel Carnival rules.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:44.250
The arena is Heartland City.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:48.470
The preliminaries start today and last for three days.

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:53.190
If you’re challenged to a duel, you must accept!

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:57.720
You’ll wager your Heart Piece in the duel.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.280
If you lose your Heart Piece, you’re eliminated.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:07.320
In order to advance to the tournament finals, you must gather and assemble five Heart Pieces.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.840
The Duel Carnival begins now!

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:16.550
Duelists, set Heartland on fire
with your passionate souls!

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:19.340
Heart Burning!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:28.600
Here I go! I’m definitely going to win!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:33.100
I’m going too!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.930
Everyone is excited.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.980
Yeah! I better not lose!

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.250
Outta the way!

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:46.030
I’ll let my friend choose my first opponent!

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.910
Are you okay?

00:21:56.630 --> 00:22:00.630
Kicking a ball here is dangerous!

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.840
It’s decided that you’re my first opponent!

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:09.330
Me?

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:23.360
Someone gave me water

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:29.490
It easily created a rainbow

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:35.200
To be who I want to be

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.230
Is difficult

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.670
Without struggle

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.900
I can’t win

00:22:46.800 --> 00:22:48.970
But I want to bloom

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:53.130
I have a dream that’s not cool

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:56.200
In order to achieve it

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:59.770
I don’t care if you laugh at me

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:06.800
I set my limits low

00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:09.830
So I’ll overcome it tomorrow

00:23:09.830 --> 00:23:14.240
Ah! Aiming for the blue skies

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:15.600
In full bloom

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.830
Yearning freesia

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.370
Countless petals

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:26.230
Were sacrificed

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:30.090
I’m above them

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.220
Ah! Lost my way again today

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.040
I admire

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:37.830
Yearning freesia

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:45.860
My first opponent is a powerful foe
who uses a soccer deck!

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:48.170
The field turned into a stadium?

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:50.540
I’ve turned into a cheerleader!

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:53.490
Yuma, what’s soccer?

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:58.790
Kakeru, you say that you hate soccer,
but don’t you actually love it?

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:01.610
I’ll make you remember that!

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:09.970
\h\hWDC Kickoff! The Flaming Striker, Kakeru Kunitachi\h\h

00:24:01.610 --> 00:24:08.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“WDC Kickoff! The Flaming Striker, Kakeru Kunitachi”

00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:16.010
Isn’t there a Number on the ground somewhere?

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:17.760
Of course not!

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:19.270
Yuma!

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:20.350
You found one?

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:22.430
You stepped in dog poop!
